# AI Security Best Practices

## Input Validation
- Validate all user input to prevent prompt injection attacks
- Implement content filtering and length limits
- Detect and handle malicious input patterns
- Implement input normalization and sanitization
- Use whitelists instead of blacklists for validation
- Implement input throttling and rate limiting
- Provide meaningful error messages for inputs that fail validation

## Data Security
- Limit agent access to sensitive data
- Implement the principle of least privilege
- Do not include sensitive information in prompts
- Anonymize user data
- Implement data encryption (in transit and at rest)
- Perform regular data access audits
- Establish data retention and deletion policies
- Comply with privacy regulations (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)

## Model Security
- Use appropriate security boundaries to limit model behavior
- Monitor and audit agent behavior
- Implement mechanisms to prevent jailbreaks
- Establish fallback strategies to handle anomalies
- Regularly evaluate the model's response to adversarial inputs
- Implement a multi-layered defense strategy
- Limit sensitive information in model responses
- Use different models for tasks with different security levels

## Third-party tool integration security
- Validate all tool inputs and outputs
- Sandbox external tool execution
- Limit API access permissions and scope
- Monitor tool usage
- Implement secure management of API keys and credentials
- Regularly update and review third-party tools
- Implement timeout and retry policies for API calls
- Use HTTPS and secure communication protocols

## Authentication and authorization
- Implement strong user authentication mechanisms
- Use multi-factor authentication
- Implement role-based access control
- Regularly review access permissions
- Set authorization boundaries for operations with different sensitivity levels
- Monitor for abnormal access patterns
- Implement session management and timeouts
- Securely store authentication credentials

## Vulnerability management
- Perform security assessments and penetration tests regularly
- Apply security patches and updates in a timely manner
- Establish vulnerability reporting and response processes
- Implement security incident monitoring and alerts
- Develop a security incident response plan
- Conduct security incident drills
- Stay on top of emerging security threats
- Participate in AI security communities and updates